{
  "about": "Background transcription queue vectors (PLAN.md section 4.9 'Queue rules', Windows 18.10), shared by the macOS and Windows apps. timing: 'immediate' | 'whenIdle' (the finalPassTiming setting). state: 'waiting' | 'running' | 'suspended' | 'done' | 'failed'. jobs are listed in queue order (first in first); ids are plain strings. sessionActive: a session is Starting, Recording, Paused, or Stopping. foregroundWaiting: number of foreground engine calls waiting (live chunks, language detection, File mode, History re-runs). A queued job may run when foregroundWaiting <= 0 and, for whenIdle, sessionActive is false. next: if a job is running, 'suspend' the first running job (queue order) when running is not allowed, else 'none'; with nothing running and running allowed, 'resume' the first suspended job, else 'start' the first waiting job, else 'none'; done and failed jobs are skipped. expect.action is start | resume | suspend | none and expect.job the job id (null for none). Invalid inputs (notes starting with 'invalid') are tolerated, never asserted: two running jobs consider only the first; a running job behind a waiting or suspended one is not preempted; a suspended job is resumed before an earlier waiting one; a negative foregroundWaiting counts as 0. shouldYield is true exactly when next would suspend a running job. presentsNotes: a finished job opens its notes flow only when no session is active and no notes flow is on screen. quitNeedsConfirmation is the count of waiting, running, and suspended jobs; blocksUpdateInstall is true when that count is above 0. Mirrors TranscriptionQueuePolicyTests.swift.",
